 "more": [
  {
   "tile": "Getting to the hostel",
   "icon": "ti-building",
   "sections": [
    {
     "heading": "Where we're staying",
     "text": "HI New York City Hostel is at 891 Amsterdam Avenue, on the corner of Amsterdam Avenue and 103rd Street."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Nearest subway",
     "text": "The nearest subway (tube) station is one block to the west, on 103rd Street and Broadway — a 2 minute walk from the hostel. The 1 train stops at this station."
    },
    {
     "heading": "2 and 3 trains",
     "text": "The 2 and 3 trains go in this direction but only stop at 96th Street. This is only a 10 minute walk from the hostel."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Distances",
     "text": "20 blocks (streets) is about a mile."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Coming back — listen!",
     "text": "When taking the subway back to the hostel, listen carefully to the announcements to make sure the train stops at 103rd Street."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Which direction?",
     "text": "• Leaving the hostel: most of the time we'll be going downtown — take trains signed Downtown & Brooklyn.\n• Coming back: take trains signed Uptown & The Bronx."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tile": "What to take",
   "icon": "ti-backpack",
   "sections": [
    {
     "heading": "Towel",
     "text": "Although all bedding is provided at the hostel you will need a towel."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Credit / debit card",
     "text": "This will be needed when using the subway. You need to use the same card every time you use the subway. By doing this you will ensure that the maximum you pay for the whole trip is $34. After this the subway rides will be free."
    },
    {
     "heading": "US adaptor",
     "text": "For charging phones etc."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Padlock",
     "text": "In your room you will have a locker. If you want to use the locker for your valuables you may want to take a padlock."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Documents & money",
     "text": "• Passport — valid for the whole trip\n• ESTA approval — school will confirm this is done\n• School ID card with the contact numbers\n• A little US cash in small notes ($1, $5, $10) for snacks and tips"
    },
    {
     "heading": "Clothes — New York in late October",
     "text": "• Warm, waterproof coat with a hood — typically around 8–16°C, colder at night and on the ferry, tram and by the rivers\n• 2 warm jumpers or hoodies for layering\n• 5 T-shirts / tops\n• 3 pairs of trousers or jeans\n• Underwear and socks for 6 days, plus spares in case your feet get wet\n• Pyjamas\n• Hat, gloves and scarf for evenings\n• Comfortable trainers that are already worn in — we walk a lot every day\n• A second pair of shoes in case one pair gets wet"
    },
    {
     "heading": "Washbag",
     "text": "• Toothbrush and toothpaste\n• Shower gel and shampoo\n• Deodorant (roll-on is easier for flights)\n• Hairbrush / comb and hair ties\n• Flip-flops for the hostel showers\n• Lip balm and hand cream — the wind can be cold\n• Hand sanitiser and tissues\n• Sanitary products if needed"
    },
    {
     "heading": "Medication",
     "text": "• Any medication you take, in its original packaging with your name on it\n• Hand it to staff as agreed with school\n• Carry inhalers / EpiPens with you, in your hand luggage — never in the hold"
    },
    {
     "heading": "Tech",
     "text": "• Phone and charger\n• Power bank, fully charged — in hand luggage only (not allowed in the hold)\n• Headphones (optional — they may be provided on the flight)\n• US adaptor (above)"
    },
    {
     "heading": "Day bag & flights",
     "text": "• A SMALL day bag or bum bag — big bags are not allowed into Madison Square Garden\n• Refillable water bottle (empty it before airport security)\n• Snacks for the flights (no peanuts — we have a peanut allergy in the group)\n• Travel pillow and a warm layer for the overnight flight home\n• A book if you like to read — the flights have in-flight entertainment, and headphones may be provided"
    },
    {
     "heading": "Room & bags",
     "text": "• Laundry bag for dirty clothes\n• Name and school label on your suitcase\n• Leave space for shopping — and check the luggage allowance with school before you pack"
    },
    {
     "heading": "Leave at home",
     "text": "• Valuable jewellery and expensive watches\n• Large amounts of cash\n• Big cameras — they won't be allowed into Madison Square Garden\n• Anything you would be upset to lose"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tile": "Safety tips",
   "icon": "ti-shield-check",
   "sections": [
    {
     "heading": "New York City",
     "text": "New York City is one of the safest cities in the USA but, like any big city, problems may arise. You must therefore follow these tips at all times."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Always",
     "text": "• NEVER travel in groups of less than 3.\n• ALWAYS follow staff instructions.\n• ALWAYS carry your identity card with you.\n• Keep your PASSPORT safe at all times.\n• Use the lockers in your room to keep your valuables safe in the hostel."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Out and about",
     "text": "• Try to avoid eye contact with beggars and anyone behaving in a strange manner.\n• DO NOT make fun of anyone who might be acting strangely.\n• Beware of pick-pockets.\n• In crowded areas, keep your valuables in your front pocket rather than the rear.\n• Keep your money and other valuables safe.\n• If you have a handbag, keep it closed and hold it tightly.\n• DO NOT flaunt jewellery, cameras, your smartphone or cash in public.\n• When in Times Square avoid having photos taken with Disney characters etc. If you do you will have to deal with demands for money!\n• Use caution if you have to use a cash machine. Inform a teacher before doing so."
    },
    {
     "heading": "If you get lost",
     "text": "If you get lost, phone one of the contact numbers on your ID card. If you need to, you may also approach a police officer or a friendly store owner to get help."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Free time",
     "text": "When given LIMITED FREE TIME make sure that you are back at the designated meeting areas on time."
    },
    {
     "heading": "On the subway",
     "text": "• Take care when getting on and off subway trains. Mind the gap between the train and the platform and be careful of opening and closing train doors.\n• Stay with your allocated group and teacher when travelling on the trains.\n• If someone is behaving in a strange manner on the train, your teacher may ask you to get off and get on the next carriage or even the next train. LISTEN TO YOUR TEACHER AT ALL TIMES WHEN TRAVELLING in case they decide to do this."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Rules",
     "text": "• NEVER cross the road unless the Walk sign is on.\n• DO NOT SMOKE OR DRINK ALCOHOL.\n• DO NOT GO INTO OTHER PEOPLE'S ROOMS."
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
